WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.733
Embodied AI and world models.

2
00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:08.433
The most heavily funded frontier in AI, and your transformer knowledge transfers directly.

3
00:00:09.633 --> 00:00:13.300
A vision language action model, or VLA, is one transformer.

4
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.167
It reads camera frames and an instruction, and outputs robot joint commands.

5
00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:23.733
Think of a VLM whose output vocabulary is motor tokens instead of words.

6
00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:26.200
Here is the pipeline.

7
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.867
Camera frames come in.

8
00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.200
Along with a plain language instruction.

9
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.333
The transformer processes both.

10
00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:35.367
And it emits motor tokens that drive the joints.

11
00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:38.100
World models add planning.

12
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.433
They learn the environment's dynamics.

13
00:00:40.733 --> 00:00:45.667
So the agent can imagine what happens if it does X, instead of learning only by trial.

14
00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:48.500
It picks the best imagined action, then acts.

15
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.067
They bridge reinforcement learning and generative modeling.

16
00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:55.667
Training happens mostly in simulation.

17
00:00:55.967 --> 00:01:02.433
Tools like Isaac Sim and MuJoCo make data free, while real robots are slow, costly, and risky.

18
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:08.133
Domain randomization varies the simulation so policies survive the reality gap.

19
00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:11.275
The scarce ingredient is data.

20
00:01:11.275 --> 00:01:14.900
There is no internet scale corpus of robot manipulation.

21
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.200
That is why teleoperation datasets and simulation get the effort.

22
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:27.233
If you want to move into this field, data is the entry point, and it is an engineering problem, not a robotics PhD problem.

23
00:01:28.433 --> 00:01:29.274
Let's recap.

24
00:01:29.274 --> 00:01:32.567
VLAs are transformers that output motor tokens.

25
00:01:32.867 --> 00:01:34.833
World models plan by imagining.

26
00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:37.767
Sim to real needs domain randomization.

27
00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:40.129
And data is your entry point.

28
00:01:40.129 --> 00:01:42.333
Next up: privacy preserving AI.
